       sortman - sort manual‐page path names

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ssoorrttmmaann

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The ssoorrttmmaann command sorts manual‐page path names in the order that they
       should appear in the manual.

       The  chapters  and  subchapters  are  first  sorted.  Then, within each
       (sub)chapter, the first page is the corresponding  iinnttrroo(*)  page,  and
       the rest are sorted alphabetically (but treating specially some special
       characters).

